@4.22 MATH.INC.BL -- the smaller and the larger of two numbers
.
=4.22 MATH.INC.BL -- THE SMALLER AND THE LARGER OF TWO NUMBERS
.
=WHAT IT COSTS
.
.    BASIC -- ordinary BASL in a .INC.BL, called with GOSUB. Free unless you
.    #INCLUDE it.
.
=DESCRIPTION
.
.  MATH.MIN
.      IN: MATH.FIRST MATH.SECOND
.      OUT: MATH.RESULT
.
.  MATH.MAX
.      IN: MATH.FIRST MATH.SECOND
.      OUT: MATH.RESULT
.
:#INCLUDE "GPB.INC.BL"
:#INCLUDE "MATH.INC.BL"
:
:MATH.FIRST = WANTED : MATH.SECOND = AVAILABLE
:GOSUB MATH.MIN
:ROWS = MATH.RESULT
.
.Both routines share all three variables. The verbs are MATH.MINOF and
.MATH.MAXOF, so the same answer comes back from GP.SUB MATH.MINOF, WANTED,
.AVAILABLE or from GP.FN(MATH.MINOF, WANTED, AVAILABLE) inside an expression.
.
.GP.FN brings the GP block in, 1,536 bytes. GOSUB and GP.SUB leave it out.
.
.Floats and integers both, and no range check. Equal arguments answer
.MATH.FIRST.
.
.A module rather than a keyword because choosing between two values needs a
.branch, and a composite cannot have one (SEC 1).
.
=SEE ALSO
.
>2|1. What GP.BASIC is
>105|4.22 MATH.INC.BL -- the smaller and the larger of two numbers
